\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Conditional next-token law}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{language-model}

\p{Let #{\Theta} be a parameter space. A \newvocab{conditional next-token
law} is a family of maps
##{
\pi_\theta:\mathcal V^*\longrightarrow\Delta(\mathcal V),
\qquad \theta\in\Theta.
}
For a prefix #{x_{<t}}, the value #{\pi_\theta(a\mid x_{<t})} is the
probability of choosing token #{a\in\mathcal V} next.}

\p{The definition records the observable probabilistic interface. It does
not yet choose the computation that produces the distribution. The
decoder-only sequence-model algorithm in
\citet{sec. 3}{phuong2022formal} has this input-output form.}
